WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.480
With Weblate, your community
or team translates repository

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.616
files, and Weblate commits them.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.799
Weblate does this well,

4
00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:10.668
with free self-hosting,

5
00:00:10.668 --> 00:00:13.685
Git workflows, and
about fifty formats.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.807
General Translation generates
translations in each release,

7
00:00:17.807 --> 00:00:19.536
with shared product context.

8
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.229
Keep your gettext files,

9
00:00:22.229 --> 00:00:24.225
and point a pot entry
at the template.

10
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.433
Then npx gt translate writes
each locale's file before you

11
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:30.048
deploy.

12
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.773
To use both, give each
language one owner,

13
00:00:33.773 --> 00:00:35.653
so neither tool
overwrites the other.

14
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.924
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
